<DocsExample TExample="BoxPlotBasicExample" Title="Box plot with outliers" Description="A box plot summarizes a distribution with its minimum, quartiles, median and maximum, and marks outliers as separate points. Use it to compare spread across groups, not only their averages." />
<DocsExample TExample="BoxPlotWidthExample" Title="Box and whisker widths" Description="BoxWidthRatio and WhiskerWidthRatio set how wide the box and the whisker caps are, as a share of the space for each category. Use narrower boxes when there are few categories." />
